m  line  none of that is true there was flooding  if we didn't have our floodgates out  back here it was within one foot  this building flooded in 2001 the whole  bottom floor  this was it would have been a safety  concern at the start but that's really  not the bigger issue is that the issue  is we work with the city they said let  us be the shelter they said go to the  county go to the city shelter so  you know somebody created a notion that  you know what we're not open in time but  they're not sitting here seeing that  the mayor's saying don't stay on the  streets don't get on the streets  that this building is a safety issue  we're here to help people we've been  doing this for 60 years so  you know that's what we're all about  here at lakewood helping the city it was  tuesday before you got really up and  running  why did it take so long to mobilize  it's if you were here you would  understand why we our volunteers people  that run this building  they can't get they can't get to the  facility we couldn't even set up our tv  hardly today  from some of our crew so you know you  just have to be here to see that  number one the city runs the shelters  what they need us to do they ask for a  distribution center and you see  hundreds and thousands of volunteers  came out they need a command center hey  you can do it here at lakewood  if you need a shelter we could have been  a shelter from day one if they wanted  that how many people have you taken in  so far  yeah i don't know how many i've lost  count but there i know there are  hundreds and  yesterday we had you know people  bringing supplies and just  you know we can't even we can hardly  take any more supplies here but  we continue to take people as many as  they bring pastor how many  can you take in and i see on your  website that you've already begun  fundraising to help the victims but  it's not clear what charity that's going  to or how it's going to be used  who are you raising money for well we'd  be  raising money for the victims here in  houston i don't know how it all works  we're working with  samaritan's purse and different ones but  we're going to be here  five years from now helping these people  we've been here for many years doing  that  so it will go to the people that are  affected by the flooding many of us many  of them are own members  are you concerned that it might be  harmful to your congregation that  there's this perception that  your church was not a sanctuary that  that even came into question in the  first place  not one bit i never paid attention to  twitter it never came up we know who we  are  if you let social media run your life in  your ministry you'll never do anything  everybody has critics that's making a  difference we know we did the right  thing for safety working with the city  and  you know that's why thousands of people  are coming out and responding now all  right pastor you've got a lot going on  behind you what is that behind you help  us  understand what is that uh we the city  asked us to be a distribution center so  people are bringing baby foods and baby  supplies and medical supplies and things  like that so  we're taking in supplies that we can  feed the different shelters around town  and so that's what they've asked us to  do and we're doing that along it's  sheltering the people here thank you  pastor for joining us  and the doors of lakewood church are  open  thanks so much gail great talking with  you all all right good to see you
 

